# WHAT THIS FILE IS READ BY, AND THE SPELLING THAT SURVIVES BOTH READERS.
# Docker matches `content/` and `content` alike. `az acr build` packs the
# context with its own reader and matches NEITHER pattern with a trailing
# slash — measured on 2026-09-02 by listing the archive it uploaded: 3,608
# files, 2,649 of them Blazor bin/obj/dist, 20 of them the client's licensed
# books, 142 MB. Every directory rule below had been inert on that path since
# the file was written; only the rules without a slash (`.env` among them,
# which is why no secret ever left) were doing anything. No trailing slashes
# here, ever.

# Secrets and local connector configuration never enter the build context.
.env
.env.*
.mcp.json

# Local environments and generated Python state.
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache

# Build products are recreated inside the image.
ui/**/bin
ui/**/obj
ui/**/dist

# Client source material stays local; production truth lives in Neon. The books
# are published volumes under copyright: they belong on her machine and in Neon
# as embeddings, and nowhere else.
content

# Developer-only state and repository metadata.
.git
.github
.claude
.vs
.vscode
.python-version
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# These do not participate in the runtime image.
docs
evals
plans
tests
nefolosite
ui/StudioViorela.Tests
LICENSE
